{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing", "label": "Composing a Workflow Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_minimum_viable_workflow", "label": "Minimum Viable Workflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fit the ceremony to the task: the least sufficient EXECUTE set that still produces every artifact the outcome depends on. Both errors are real - skipping a load-bearing stage has a cost someone pays later, and including overlapping ceremony just in case collapses a composed grid back toward the stock feature scope and defeats composing. Neither default caution nor default economy is acceptable."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_entropy_scoring", "label": "Entropy Scoring Before Selection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "How to read a task", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Estimate the five components (intent ambiguity, structural uncertainty, verification entropy, risk, unresolved assumptions) BEFORE looking at any stock scope, because the component bands rather than keyword vibes determine which stages carry positive expected value."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_incremental_vs_net_new", "label": "Incremental versus Net-New Task Shape", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "How to read a task", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Work inside an existing system needs to understand what exists, define done, and change-plus-verify; it does not need market-research, user-stories, or application-design, because those discover and shape a product that already exists. Net-new surface needs the discovery arc in proportion to how much new structure it introduces."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_operational_outcome", "label": "Operational Outcome Trigger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "How to read a task", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deployment, observability, incident-response and performance stages belong on the plan when the task's DONE lives in an environment rather than in the repo - a plan that builds but never ships closes no operational task."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_brownfield_vs_greenfield", "label": "Brownfield versus Greenfield Grid Effect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "How to read a task", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The classification changes the WHOLE grid, not one stage: a brownfield feature leans on existing structure and can compress discovery, while a greenfield feature has nothing to reverse-engineer and everything to scope."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_grid_discipline", "label": "Grid Discipline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "Grid discipline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every required consume must have its producer on the EXECUTE set (validator-enforced, rejected in in-flight strict mode), and a starved input is never silently balanced by adding the producer - the addition is named in the rationale so the human sees the plan grow and why. Stages are data-coupled, so consumes/produces are checked before cutting anything mid-arc."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_fold_overlapping_stages", "label": "Folding Overlapping Stages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "Grid discipline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "When two stages reduce the same entropy component, keep the spine (core, verification, and the single load-bearing discovery/design stage) and fold the framing stage whose output another EXECUTE stage already delivers - naming the un-SKIP trigger. Prefer a stock scope within a couple of stage flips, because a custom scope is maintenance surface the user owns forever."}, {"id": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_rationale_quality", "label": "Rationale Quality Standard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": "Rationale quality", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gate is only as good as the rationale, so each SKIP gets one vetoable line naming the stage, what it would have produced, and why this task does not need that artifact; each EXECUTE names the component it reduces and that no other EXECUTE stage delivers that reduction. Not needed is not a rationale."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing", "target": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing_minimum_viable_workflow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": ".claude/knowledge/aidlc-composer-agent/composing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "_claude_knowledge_aidlc_composer_agent_composing", "target": "_claude_knowl